<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n86298" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρέσβ-ις</span></b>  (B), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, poet. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρεσβεία,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>age,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ πρέσβιν</span> according to <i>age,
				h. Merc.</i><i><span class="en">
				431
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				855d
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>aged woman,</i>
			
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρεσβῦτις</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Aesop.
				107b
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				pp.182,183
			</span></i> Chambry). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>ambassadress,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ael.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				738.62
			</span></i>.</div>
